# Optional during local development; required for hosted CMS image authorization,
# native public form Origin checks and the canonical EmDash origin.
# Set the actual site origin in the production build environment.
# SITE_URL=https://your-site.example

# Generate EmDash secrets into your ignored .env with:
# npx emdash secrets generate --write .env

# Optional build-time page redirects; enable only after checking lowercase slugs
# and custom endpoint exclusions. Never normalize asset or CMS storage URLs.
# NORMALIZE_PAGE_URLS=1

# Optional build-time Content-Security-Policy for public pages, computed from each
# page's inline scripts and styles. Start with report (blocks nothing; check the
# console and npm run check:quality), then enforce. Add third-party origins with
# CSP_SOURCES, for example Cloudflare Web Analytics:
# CSP_MODE=report

# Optional analytics (src/components/Analytics.astro), loaded only on the production
# hostnames listed. Cloudflare Web Analytics is cookie-free; GA4/GTM start under
# Google Consent Mode v2 with everything denied and show the consent banner
# (PUBLIC_CONSENT_MODE=strict loads nothing before consent). Bump
# PUBLIC_CONSENT_VERSION to ask every visitor again. With a CSP, add the origins:
# CSP_SOURCES="script-src https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.openstreetmap.org"
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_HOSTS=example.ch,www.example.ch
# PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=
# PUBLIC_GA_ID=
# PUBLIC_GTM_ID=
# PUBLIC_CONSENT_MODE=consent-mode
# PUBLIC_CONSENT_VERSION=1
# CSP_SOURCES="script-src https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src https://cloudflareinsights.com"
